.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NQDPACK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdpack ,
.Nm nqdunpack
.Nd a capsule in one file, and back
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqdpack "const char *dir" "int files" "const char *file"
.Ft int
.Fo nqdunpack
.Fa "const char *file" "const char *dir" "int rm" "char *why" "size_t cap"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqdpack
writes the sealed capsule
.Fa dir
to the new
.Fa file
as a bundle
.Pq Ql noqtis-bundle-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5 :
its
.Pa noqtis.json ,
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
.Pa noqtis.ers
when there is one, and every file its manifest lists
.Pq Fa files No 1 ,
or of those only its data record
.Pa noqtis.data.json
.Pq Fa files No 0 ,
in the byte order of their paths.
The same folder gives the same bytes.
.Fa file
must not exist; on any error it is removed again.
Nothing is checked: check the capsule with
.Xr nqchk 3
first.
.Pp
.Fn nqdunpack
reads the bundle
.Fa file
into the new folder
.Fa dir ,
which it makes.
The reader is strict, and refuses the bundle whole, removing everything
it wrote and
.Fa dir ,
for: a file that does not start with the format's line; a path that is
not one a capsule holds (empty, absolute, with
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql \&.. ,
a backslash, a colon, so no drive letter, a control character, invalid
UTF-8, a NUL) or that is over 64 folders deep, and on Windows a name the
system takes for a device
.Pq Ql CON , Ql NUL , Ql COM1 , ...
or one ending in a dot or space; paths out of order or given twice;
no
.Pa noqtis.json
or
.Pa noqtis.sig ;
a bundle cut short or with bytes after its end; a path over 4096 bytes,
more than 2,000,003 entries, a file over 2^53 \- 1 bytes, a seal over
1 MiB or a manifest over 512 MiB.
Every file is created new, never over one that is there or through a
link, and every folder is made by
.Fn nqdunpack
inside
.Fa dir ,
so no path leaves it; two paths that differ only in case on a file
system that ignores case are refused.
Check
.Fa dir
afterwards with
.Xr nqchk 3 ;
when the bundle carries only the data record, check that alone
.Po
.Xr nqchkx 3
with
.Fa only
.Pc .
.Pp
With
.Fa rm
1,
.Fn nqdunpack
removes instead what an unpack of the same
.Fa file
wrote to
.Fa dir ,
then
.Fa dir
when it is empty; nothing else is removed.
.Pp
.Fa why ,
when not
.Dv NULL ,
gets a sentence
.Pf ( Fa cap
bytes) on what was refused.
.Ss Format
.Bd -literal -offset indent
"noqtis-bundle-1\en"                   16 bytes
then per file: path length   2 bytes, big-endian, 1 to 4096
               path          UTF-8, a capsule path
               size          8 bytes, big-endian
               bytes         size bytes
then the end:  0x00 0x00
.Ed
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ;
.Dv NQEARG
for a
.Dv NULL
argument,
.Fa files
or
.Fa rm
not 0 or 1, or
.Fa files
0 for a capsule that lists no data record;
.Dv NQEIO
when
.Fa file
exists
.Pq Fn nqdpack ,
.Fa dir
exists
.Pq Fn nqdunpack ,
or a file cannot be read or written;
.Dv NQEDEC
and
.Dv NQELIM
for a bundle refused as above;
.Dv NQEMEM .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-export 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-pack 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqfiles 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
